; roundto_commodity() -- the function behind --round -- physically rounds
; the stored value to its commodity's precision (half away from zero), so
; unrounded() cannot bring the dropped digits back.  rounded() only clears
; keep_precision: unrounded(rounded(x)) shows every digit again (#3220).
; This covers amount_t::in_place_round_to_commodity_precision and its
; value_t AMOUNT, BALANCE and SEQUENCE dispatch.
;
; CHF appears only inside a price annotation, so the journal gives it no
; precision.  The cost 20 * 5.025 CHF = 100.500 CHF keeps its precision,
; so roundto_commodity() has no precision to round to and must leave the
; fraction alone rather than print it as CHF100 or CHF101 (#3187).  The
; last two blocks reach that guard through roundto_commodity(cost) and
; through --round over --basis.

2024/01/01 Setup
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Expenses:Food    10.00 EUR
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 Buy
    Assets:Crypto    20 ETH @ 5.025 CHF
    Assets:Cash

test reg Food --format '%(unrounded(roundto_commodity(amount * 0.1255)))|%(unrounded(roundto_commodity(-amount * 0.1255)))|%(unrounded(rounded(amount * 0.1255)))\n'
$1.26|$-1.26|$1.255
1.26 EUR|-1.26 EUR|1.255 EUR
end test

test bal Food --balance-format '%(unrounded(roundto_commodity(total * 0.1255)))\n---\n'
$1.26
1.26 EUR
---
end test

test reg Food --format '%(unrounded(roundto_commodity(to_sequence(amount * 0.1255))))\n'
($1.26)
(1.26 EUR)
end test

test reg Crypto --format '%(roundto_commodity(cost))\n'
CHF100.5
end test

test reg Crypto --round -B
24-Jan-02 Buy                   Assets:Crypto              CHF100.5     CHF100.5
end test
